.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECURESPF-CHECK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securespf-check
.Nd command-line SPF evaluation tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl i Ar ip-address
.Fl s Ar sender
.Op Fl e Ar helo-domain
.Op Fl n Ar nameserver
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
performs a one-shot SPF evaluation for the given client IP and sender address,
printing the result to standard output.
It uses the same SPF evaluation engine as
.Xr securespf 8
but runs as a standalone command without requiring a running milter.
.Pp
This is useful for testing SPF records, debugging delivery issues, and
verifying DNS configuration.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl i Ar ip-address
Client IP address (IPv4 or IPv6) to evaluate.
Required.
.It Fl s Ar sender
MAIL FROM address (e.g.,
.Dq user@example.com ) .
Required.
.It Fl e Ar helo-domain
EHLO/HELO domain.
If not specified, extracted from the sender address.
.It Fl n Ar nameserver
DNS nameserver IP address.
Default:
.Dq 127.0.0.1 .
.It Fl h
Display usage information.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It 0
SPF result is
.Dq pass .
.It 1
SPF result is
.Dq fail ,
.Dq softfail ,
.Dq neutral ,
.Dq none ,
.Dq temperror ,
or
.Dq permerror .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check an IPv4 sender:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securespf-check -i 192.168.1.233 -s user@bambania.com
.Ed
.Pp
Check with explicit HELO and custom DNS:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securespf-check -i 203.0.113.1 -s bounce@example.com -e mail.example.com -n 8.8.8.8
.Ed
.Pp
Check an IPv6 sender:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securespf-check -i 2001:db8::1 -s user@example.org
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securespf 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T Sender Policy Framework (SPF) for Authorizing Use of Domains in Email
.%R RFC 7208
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
